  "id": "0012-an-anchor-keeps-the-first-narrowest-bracket-and-states-its-error",
  "about": "Anchor::from_brackets(brackets, monotonic_resolution_ns, monotonic, wall_source, wall_resolution_ns, wall_rounding). Brackets are [m1, wall_unix_ns, m2]. A bracket with wall 0 or m2 < m1 is discarded; of the rest the smallest m2 - m1 is kept, the first on a tie; none left is none. monotonic_ns is m1 + floor(s/2) and read_span_ns is s. The bound is the anchor error on wall_unix_ns: early = ceil(s/2) + mono late + wall early, late = floor(s/2) + mono early + wall late, from bound_for_read of each leg, saturating; either resolution none gives UNBOUNDED on both sides with basis Unspecified (0), otherwise basis ClockRead (9). A face that uses the span alone fails native_worked and zero_span; keeps the last of a tie fails first_narrowest_on_a_tie; uses m2 as the anchor point fails every row with a span; ignores a two-sided leg fails the two_sided rows. wall_source is passed through and does not enter any value here.",
